{% icon id="sword-clash" size=32 /%}Know about every attack before it lands. Discord attack alerts has two {% term id="plugin" %}plugins{% /term %}, each on its own tab of the module page. Both post to Discord channels you choose.

- **Incoming attacks** posts a message when a player attacks you or your alliance.
- **Outgoing attacks** posts the attacks your alliance sends.

## Incoming attacks {% #incoming %}

The bot posts a message when a player attacks one of your castles. It also posts when a player outside your alliance attacks a member of your alliance.

Each message names:

- The attacker, their castle and their alliance.
- The player under attack and their castle.
- The kingdom and the distance between the two castles, in clicks.
- A live countdown to the moment the attack lands.

When the game shows the attacking army, the bot adds a picture of the army's layout to the message.

### Mentions {% #mentions %}

The bot looks for a member of the channel whose Discord display name is exactly the name of the player under attack. If it finds one, the message mentions that member.

If that member is not online and not on Do Not Disturb, the bot mentions them up to four more times before the attack lands. It skips a mention while they are online or on Do Not Disturb. It does not repeat mentions for attacks on the Storm Islands.

Turn on **Mention everyone** to add @everyone to each message.

{% aside type="tip" id="match-names" %}
Ask your alliance members to set their Discord nickname to their game name. Then each one gets a mention when they are attacked.
{% /aside %}

### Storm Islands channel {% #storm-channel %}

Attacks on the Storm Islands go to **Storm Islands channel ID**, not to the first channel. If you leave it empty, the bot does not post Storm Islands attacks at all.

{% settings plugin="incomingAttacks" /%}

## Outgoing attacks {% #outgoing %}

The bot posts each attack that leaves your alliance for a player outside it. That includes your own attacks and the attacks of your alliance members that your bot can see.

Each message names the two players and their castles, the alliance of the player under attack, the kingdom, the distance in clicks, and a live countdown. It always comes with a picture of the attacking army's layout. The bot posts each attack one time.

{% settings plugin="outgoingAttacks" /%}

## Connect a Discord channel {% #channel-id %}

GGE Command posts through its own Discord bot. You don't need a webhook. You give the module the ID of the channel to post in.

1. Make sure the GGE Command Discord bot is a member of your Discord, and that it can see and post in the channel.
2. In Discord, open **User Settings**, then **Advanced**, and turn on **Developer Mode**.
3. Right-click the channel and choose **Copy Channel ID**.
4. Paste the ID into **Channel ID** on the plugin's tab, then save.
5. Start the bot if it is not running.

The field takes only the ID, a long number. A channel name or a link does not work.

{% aside type="note" id="discord-bot-access" %}
Not sure whether the GGE Command Discord bot can reach your channel? [Contact us](/contact/) before you set up the channels.
{% /aside %}

## Tips and limits {% #tips %}

- The plugins post only while your bot is online.
- Give each plugin its own channel, so incoming and outgoing attacks don't mix.
- The [Messages](/modules/messages/) and [Discord event alerts](/modules/discord-events/) modules use the same kind of channel ID.
